id: pm-vcs-hi5k
title: Fetch with object negotiation computed from reachability
description: "Fetch must not send the whole object store. The client offers the commits it already has as candidates, the remote keeps only the ones it actually holds, and the bundle it builds excludes everything reachable from that agreed set and declares it as a prerequisite instead. The branches a fetch learns land on tracking refs; tags keep their own names, because a tag identifies a point in history rather than one repository's opinion about a line of work. Publishing the remote's own branch names, which is what a plain bundle import does, would move the local branch of the same name onto the remote's tip and silently discard whatever the local agent had committed there."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:vcs",distribution
